{"name":"Alligator Egg","hex":"#eaeed7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alligator","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Either of two species of large amphibious reptile, Alligator mississippiensis or Alligator sinensis, in the genus Alligator within order Crocodilia, which have sharp teeth and very strong jaws and are native to the Americas and China, respectively.","A crocodilian of the subfamily Alligatorinae."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To crack in a pattern resembling an alligator's skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alligator"},{"term":"egg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food.","An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something).","To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alligator meat","blocks":[{"text":"Alligator meat is the meat from alligators that is for consumption. In the Southern United States, alligator meat is commonly eaten, where it is regarded as a delicacy and staple in local cuisines both historically and in modern times. Alligator eggs can also be consumed. Alligator meat is high in protein and low in fat, and has a mild flavor and firm texture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Fried_Gator_Tail_%28505318016%29.jpg/330px-Fried_Gator_Tail_%28505318016%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alligator_meat"},{"title":"Alligator","blocks":[{"text":"An alligator, or colloquially gator, is a large reptile in the genus Alligator of the family Alligatoridae in the order Crocodilia. The two extant species are the American alligator and the Chinese alligator. Additionally, several extinct species of alligator are known from fossil remains. Alligators first appeared during the late Eocene epoch about 37 million years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Chinese%2Bamerican_alligators.png/330px-Chinese%2Bamerican_alligators.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alligator"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Blackened_Alligator_at_Felix.jpg/500px-Blackened_Alligator_at_Felix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Blackened_Alligator_at_Felix.jpg/1280px-Blackened_Alligator_at_Felix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Blackened_Alligator_at_Felix.jpg/500px-Blackened_Alligator_at_Felix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blackened alligator at Felix's restaurant in New Orleans, Louisiana, United States","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlackened_Alligator_at_Felix.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Smoked_alligator_jerky_at_a_store_in_--Richfield%2C_Wisconsin--.jpg/500px-Smoked_alligator_jerky_at_a_store_in_--Richfield%2C_Wisconsin--.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Smoked_alligator_jerky_at_a_store_in_--Richfield%2C_Wisconsin--.jpg/1280px-Smoked_alligator_jerky_at_a_store_in_--Richfield%2C_Wisconsin--.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Smoked_alligator_jerky_at_a_store_in_--Richfield%2C_Wisconsin--.jpg/500px-Smoked_alligator_jerky_at_a_store_in_--Richfield%2C_Wisconsin--.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Smoked alligator jerky at a store in Richfield, Wisconsin, United States","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmoked_alligator_jerky_at_a_store_in_--Richfield%2C_Wisconsin--.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Alligator_eggs_and_young_alligators.jpg/500px-Alligator_eggs_and_young_alligators.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Alligator_eggs_and_young_alligators.jpg/1280px-Alligator_eggs_and_young_alligators.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f